== 4. the coincidence (logs/engine_speed.log, laptop, 14 November 2026); recorded, not used by the rule
  garbagecollector: slowest level 94 expansions per second, rank 1 of 26 confirmatory games from the slowest; levels whose bound reaches the time cap: 5 of 5
  the slowest game that fits: lasers, 255 expansions per second; games that fit with a level whose bound reaches the time cap: 0
  the laptop bound for 2,000,000 states, summed over the levels of all 26 games before the rule (per-level bounds as printed in logs/engine_speed.log, each rounded to the second): 372343 worker-seconds, 3.23 sessions of 115200 worker-seconds
  the laptop bound for 2,000,000 states, summed over the levels of the 25 games after the rule (per-level bounds as printed in logs/engine_speed.log, each rounded to the second): 300343 worker-seconds, 2.61 sessions of 115200 worker-seconds
  the rule's reason is the frame: a grid wider than 64 columns or taller than 62 rows cannot be presented to the agents at one cell per level cell; the speed of a game plays no part in it

